@startuml compiled-binding-sources
!theme plain
title Sources used for compiled PLC bindings
actor "Control Studio engine (setupDiscover)" as engine
actor "Plant editor (HMI Builder, network canvas)" as ui
participant "LSP command handler\ntrust-lsp command hmiBindings" as command
participant "load_hmi_sources_edited" as loader
participant "Runtime compiler" as compiler
engine -> command : Request compiled bindings\n(a separate command-line run; no language server session)
ui -> command : Request compiled bindings\n(language server command)
command -> loader : Read project ST sources: open editor text when the call names it, else the disk
loader -> loader : Exclude files with @trustlsp:runtime-ignore\nin their first 20 lines
loader --> command : Runtime sources only
command -> compiler : Compile retained sources
alt Runtime source error
  compiler --> command : Compile error
  command --> engine : Explain error; no catalog
  command --> ui : Explain error; no catalog
else Successful compilation
  compiler --> command : Runtime metadata
  command -> command : Process image: commands (outputs), feedbacks (inputs) and memory\nlist the numeric signals, SINT to LREAL; booleans list every addressed BOOL\nbit of inputs, outputs and memory, such as %MX40.0
  note right of command
    A declared BOOL state is a catalog signal (B1.3, booleans);
    the plant candidates stay numeric.
  end note
  command --> engine : Configured PLC bindings and catalog signals
  command --> ui : Configured PLC bindings
end
@enduml
